"Let $a$ and $b$ be positive integers satisfying\n\n$$\n\\gcd(a,b)=1,\n$$\n\nwith $a$ and $b$ not both odd. An $(a,b)$ knight's tour is a cycle visiting every vertex of the corresponding knight's graph on $[n]^d$ exactly once. **Erde, Golé nia and Golé nia's conjecture.** For sufficiently large even $n$ and $d\\geq 2$, there is an $(a,b)$ knight's tour in $[n]^d$.\n\nThe conjecture proposes a general existence criterion for generalized knight's tours under the necessary parity and coprimality conditions. The stated question of necessary conditions for existence of an $(a,1)$ knight's tour for even $a$ remains open."